<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Resources this app names at runtime, from Dart, and nowhere else.

  The release build runs Android's resource shrinker, which keeps a resource
  only when it can see a reference to it from Java or from XML. A name that
  exists solely as a string handed to a plugin — `@drawable/ic_stat_deltoid`
  for the notification's small icon, `rest_done` for the alert tone — looks
  like a resource nobody wants, and it is deleted.

  What that cost: every release build ever made shipped without the rest tone,
  so the alert that ends a rest was silent on a phone in a pocket while the
  in-app tone — a Flutter asset, which the shrinker never sees — played
  perfectly with the app open. The icon joined it in 1.3.0, and a notification
  whose icon resource does not exist cannot be posted at all, which took the
  whole session line down with it.

  Anything added here must also be added to the list in
  `test/tools/kept_resources_test.dart`, which reads this file and the Dart
  that names them, and fails when the two disagree.
-->
<resources
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@drawable/ic_stat_deltoid,@raw/rest_done" />
